WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.597
After your ONT run: Start a new methylation-only project. This is the real UI with synthetic files; no analysis is run.

2
00:00:05.597 --> 00:00:12.349
Original sample membership: Choose preservation from specimen records, then discover the original barcode FASTQs. These are synthetic examples.

3
00:00:12.349 --> 00:00:27.517
Name the samples: These fictional tumour samples have leukemia, CNS or unknown clinical context. Assign the main sample role first.

4
00:00:27.517 --> 00:00:34.300
Use original methylation calls: Keep methylation-only analysis. Link the original modified-base BAMs with MM/ML tags, not an ordinary CNA alignment.

5
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:43.425
POD5 is the alternative: POD5 requires compatible Dorado basecalling and modified-base models. Existing modified-base BAMs avoid basecalling again.

6
00:00:43.425 --> 00:00:54.280
Drag from documented clinical context: Drag leukemia to MARLIN and CNS tumour to Sturgeon. A previous classifier prediction is not the selection rule.

7
00:00:54.280 --> 00:01:00.299
Unknown stays unassigned: Leave unknown or unsuitable clinical context unassigned. The dropdown on each card offers the same accessible choice.

8
00:01:00.299 --> 00:01:16.154
Reuse local tools and reference: Supply installed tool and model paths, or a resource YAML. This demonstration uses synthetic path fixtures, not trained models.

9
00:01:16.154 --> 00:01:22.714
One classifier per project: Choose MARLIN. Only its assigned sample enters this project; the other two are excluded and are not queued.

10
00:01:22.714 --> 00:01:27.076
Separate destination: Save to a new cpg-marlin project. Keep the completed ONT project and the other classifier's project unchanged.

11
00:01:27.076 --> 00:01:34.873
Save and check only: Save the selected group's configuration and inspect the included names. These checks validate synthetic paths, not biological model quality.

12
00:01:34.873 --> 00:01:41.401
One classifier per project: Choose Sturgeon. Only its assigned sample enters this project; the other two are excluded and are not queued.

13
00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.294
Sturgeon resources and license: Use your installed Sturgeon assets and confirm its terms only after accepting them. This checkbox is demonstrated with synthetic fixtures.

14
00:01:43.294 --> 00:01:47.759
Separate destination: Save to a new cpg-sturgeon project. Keep the completed ONT project and the other classifier's project unchanged.

15
00:01:47.759 --> 00:01:55.557
Save and check only: Save the selected group's configuration and inspect the included names. These checks validate synthetic paths, not biological model quality.

16
00:01:55.557 --> 00:02:03.458
Ready for a real project: Resolve errors before Run analysis in your real project. Review CpG coverage and classifier scores afterward. This recording ends without running analysis.
